    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DtCMR6qcoYVuswMQFkPCKF)_\n\nAdds `rel-anno-fa2` to `sp-graphs`: the relationship annotator's scope drawn as a ForceAtlas2 graph in an Emacs buffer with [elij/graph-fa2](https://github.com/elij/graph-fa2).\n\n**How I read the request:** a new force-directed view next to the existing browser graph (which is unchanged), because graph-fa2 draws SVG in a buffer rather than in a browser.\n\n- `graph-fa2` is installed with `use-package` and Elpaca `:ensure (:host github :repo \"elij/graph-fa2\")`; edge labels on, label wrap 18.\n- Same starting note and depth prompt, same scope as the browser graph.\n- Depth: node radius shrinks with the level below the start (`relationship-annotator-fa2-radius`, 18 down to 7); last-level nodes show `(+N)` hidden children.\n- Nodes show the title and `#tags` instead of plain dots.\n- Links show the relation (`parent`, `supports`, ...) in the relation's colour, as arrows.\n- Node fill comes from the tag group of the first grouped tag (`sp-org-tag-group-of`, `sp-org-tag-groups-colors`, `sp-org-tag-groups-palette`), light or dark by frame background.\n- Clicking a node visits the note.\n- Literate doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\nNot run: the container has no Emacs, so this was only read against graph-fa2's source. Worth checking in a real session: that tags wrap legibly, that the label colour reads on your theme, and that the click hook fires.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9MFEtBRvJfg7M7vTd)_",
